\pard\plain \sa180\sb180\ltrch\loch {By the time I reached the last bend in the road, my legs were on fire. The kind of burn that makes you swear you\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92re pedaling through wet cement instead of gravel. Sweat clung to the inside of my collar, and every breath felt like I was drinking the air instead of breathing it.}
\par\plain {The Academy loomed ahead, its stone towers stabbing up from the hillside like smug fingers pointing out just how far I still had to go.}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Unbelievable,\u8221\'94 I muttered between gulps of air. \u8220\'93How in the world did younger me do this every single morning and still have the energy to sit through lectures?\u8221\'94 I barely had the strength to keep the handlebars straight, let alone imagine opening a textbook after this uphill torture.}
\par\plain {Back then, I used to roll into class bright-eyed, legs of steel, probably thinking I was immortal. Now? Now I felt like I\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d aged fifty years since last week\u8217\'92s birthday. My thighs were staging a rebellion, and honestly, I wasn\u8217\'92t sure I could blame them.}
\par\plain {I coasted the last few meters, slowing just enough to make it look like I\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d }{\f0\fs24\i1 meant}{ to crawl up the hill instead of collapse at the gates. Dignity first. Breathing second.}}